The test failure is fixed. Build, the full test suite (19 test binaries, all passing), clippy with -D warnings, and the format check are all clean.

Why it failed: the yoagent 0.25.2 upgrade changed this behaviour; yoyo's code is fine. The 0.25.2 CHANGELOG says an Anthropic in-stream overloaded_error is now treated as RateLimited. That error type carries no message, so it shows as "Rate limited". The test's last check looked for the provider's own word "Overloaded" in stderr, and that text never reaches yoyo now. The captured stderr confirms it: error: Rate limited and (failed after 6 attempts).

Fix: one edit in tests/print_stdout_contract.rs. In opt_in_every_attempt_dying_after_text_terminates_nonzero_within_the_cap, the check now looks for "Rate limited" instead of "Overloaded". A comment above it records the old assertion as superseded (0.25.2 upgrade, Day 225, #1007) and cites the CHANGELOG entry.

Something you should know: this means editing a test's expected text to match new behaviour. It's justified by yoagent's documented change, not by a guess. The test still checks the same three things it did before:
• the run fails with a nonzero exit
• yoyo's own retry cap is reported
• stderr names the failure

The provider's explanation text is lost, though. yoagent now logs it at WARN instead, so a user seeing this error gets "Rate limited" where they used to get "Overloaded". The other two "Overloaded" checks in the file (lines 788 and 793) also accept a generic "error", so I left them alone.
